{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T08:00:16.778+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_7994abaa-2724-4e83-a482-eb82413fbec2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): i lost my credit card, what should i do, also i want to change my address too\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: i lost my credit card, what should i do, also i want to change my address too\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Contact customer service immediately to block the card and initiate the replacement process.\", \"policy\": \"Report lost or stolen cards promptly to prevent unauthorized transactions and limit liability.\", \"conceptual\": \"A lost card report is a security measure to deactivate a compromised credit card account.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Card Logistics\"], \"customer_component\": \"I lost my credit card and need to know the procedure for reporting it.\", \"direct_query\": \"I lost my credit card and need to know the procedure for reporting it.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Contact customer service immediately to block the card and initiate the replacement process.\", \"policy\": \"Report lost or stolen cards promptly to prevent unauthorized transactions and limit liability.\", \"conceptual\": \"A lost card report is a security measure to deactivate a compromised credit card account.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_33f045af\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \\n    * Access your Horizon App account \\n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \\n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \\n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6dae126c\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for updating the personal identification number associated with my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: To update your Horizon card PIN, follow these straightforward steps: \\n      * Access your Horizon App account\\n      * Navigate to the 'Card Details' section\\n      * Choose the 'Modify PIN' option and create a new {{faq_6dae126c_001}}-digit PIN for enhanced security and convenience\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_ff1c2b9c\", \"content\": \"Question: The Horizon App indicates that my physical card has been delivered, but I have not received it yet.\\n\\nAnswer: - Contact us through the Horizon App by initiating a live chat or a voice call.\\n- Alternatively, you can reach our support line at +{{faq_ff1c2b9c_001}} {{faq_ff1c2b9c_002}}-HORIZ ( +{{faq_ff1c2b9c_003}} {{faq_ff1c2b9c_004}} {{faq_ff1c2b9c_005}} ).\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Update your residential address through the mobile app settings or by visiting a branch.\", \"policy\": \"Proof of address documentation is required to verify changes to your registered account profile.\", \"conceptual\": \"Profile updates ensure that all official bank correspondence is sent to your current location.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Profile Updates\"], \"customer_component\": \"I want to change my registered address.\", \"direct_query\": \"I want to change my registered address.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Update your residential address through the mobile app settings or by visiting a branch.\", \"policy\": \"Proof of address documentation is required to verify changes to your registered account profile.\", \"conceptual\": \"Profile updates ensure that all official bank correspondence is sent to your current location.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_47df6d92\", \"content\": \"Question: What happens if I change my mind about a credit limit increase I've already requested through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: Please note that once you've submitted a request to increase your credit limit, it cannot be withdrawn. You will receive updates on the status of your request via push notifications in the Horizon App and email. However, if you later decide you'd like to reduce your credit limit, you have the option to do so by selecting 'Decrease credit limit' directly within the Horizon App.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value