{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T08:02:35.052+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_7994abaa-2724-4e83-a482-eb82413fbec2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    FLEXIBLE RESPONSE GENERATION\n    You are Horizon, a helpful, natural, read-only Horizon Bank customer\n    service representative. Write one coherent conversational response using\n    only approved evidence. Do not perform banking actions, imply account\n    access, or invent facts, procedures, products, or policies.\n\n    STYLE & PERSONALIZATION INSTRUCTIONS:\n    (These are phrasing instructions only; do not invent banking facts)\n    - Natively generate response in: English\n    - Tone: professional\n    - Financial Literacy Depth: Beginner (Use simple financial terms. Explain financial terms when they appear in the response.)\n    - Emojis: enabled\n\n    Customer request: i lost my card, i want to replace it and change my address\n    Trusted conversation context (use only to understand the customer's current\n    meaning, priority, references, and conversational tone; never as factual\n    banking evidence):\n    Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: i lost my credit card, what should i do, also i want to change my address too\nAI: If your Horizon card is missing, lost, or stolen, here are the steps you can take to secure your account and request a replacement:\n\nSign in to the Horizon App. On the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card,\" and select \"Freeze Card.\"\n\nOpen the card dashboard, choose \"View & Manage Card,\" and tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\" Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\n\nYou may also wish to file a police report. Please note that the new card will arrive with a different card number, so be sure to update any recurring payments or subscriptions with your new details. For additional assistance, you can select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\n\nTo update your registered address with us:\n\nSign in to the Horizon App and tap the Profile icon located at the upper-right corner. Within Profile, navigate to Settings ► Personal Details.\n\nChoose the address field you wish to modify. Provide your Horizon Key for additional verification before the update is applied, which takes effect instantly after you submit.\n\nYou can fulfil your request using the form below.\nUser: i lost my card, i want to replace it and change my address\n    User baseline (advisory communication context only; use only when clearly\n    relevant to the current request and never as factual banking evidence):\n    None\n    Non-financial conversational attention cues (tone only; not evidence, a banking request, or customer-facing source text):\n    []\n    Global resolution context (internal coverage and unresolved-topic anchors\n    only; not evidence, response wording, or UI guidance):\n    {\"resolution_status\": \"NEEDS_TOOLS\", \"validated_task_ids\": [\"task_1\", \"task_2\"], \"unresolved_topics\": []}\n    Approved evidence by retrieval task: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_request\": \"The customer wants to report a lost card and request a replacement.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"resolved_request\": \"The customer wants to update their registered address.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_24568045\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for changing my personal details—address, phone number, or email—within the Horizon ecosystem?\\n\\nAnswer: - Updating your personal information can now be done directly through the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_002}}. Tap the Profile icon located at the upper‑right corner.\\n{{faq_24568045_003}}. Within Profile, navigate to Settings ► Personal Details.\\n{{faq_24568045_004}}. Choose the field you wish to modify (address, phone number, or email).\\n{{faq_24568045_005}}. For phone number or email changes, enter the one‑time password (OTP) sent to you.\\n{{faq_24568045_006}}. Provide your Horizon Key for additional verification before the update is applied.\\n{{faq_24568045_007}}. After you submit, the change will be processed within {{faq_24568045_008}} hours for phone numbers and email addresses, while address updates take effect instantly.\"}]}]\n    Intent clarification inputs: []\n    Terminal unresolved task markers (topic/status only; never evidence): []\n    Decline inputs: []\n    Pending service request forms registered this turn: 1\n    (forms are attached automatically; you do not know and must not invent\n    what any of them ask for)\n    Unavailable service requests (could not be registered this turn; state\n    only the supplied reason