age Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}]}]\n    Intent clarification inputs: []\n    Terminal unresolved task markers (topic/status only; never evidence): [{\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"type\": \"TERMINAL_RETRIEVAL_FEEDBACK\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"I want to resubmit my KYC documentation.\", \"resolution_status\": \"CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED\"}]\n    Decline inputs: []\n    Pending service request forms registered this turn: 2\n    (forms are attached automatically; you do not know and must not invent\n    what any of them ask for)\n    Unavailable service requests (could not be registered this turn; state\n    only the supplied reason, never guess why): []\n    Failed outbound-audit feedback (constraints only, never evidence). Each\n    entry identifies one specific claim or instruction to remove — it is\n    never permission to abandon the topic it came from. After removing\n    exactly what is flagged, re-apply every Design Principle below to still\n    give the most complete, honestly-scoped response the remaining approved\n    evidence supports:\n    []\n\n    \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact a