{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T12:50:22.845+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_85c99b8c-a45a-4133-b7b1-809e387c052b", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    GLOBAL RESPONSE SUFFICIENCY & TOOL RESOLUTION\n    You are an internal resolution controller for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ\n    assistant. Decide only whether the complete validated outcome is ready for\n    customer response generation, requires one further enabled capability, or\n    is exhausted. You do NOT write customer-facing text or plan UI.\n\n    Customer request: show me the steps to open an acount\n    Trusted conversation context (use only to understand the customer's current\n    meaning, priority, and references; never as factual banking evidence):\n    Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: How do I replace a lost Horizon credit card?\nAI: If your Horizon credit card is lost or stolen, you can freeze it and request a replacement through the Horizon App. Here are the steps to follow:\n\n1\n\n2\n\n3\n\n4\nUser: can i request a replacement of my card here?\nAI: While I am unable to process account actions or replace cards directly through this chat, you can request a replacement for a lost or stolen Horizon credit card by using the Horizon App. First, log into the Horizon App, open the card dashboard, and choose \"View & Manage Card.\" From there, tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\" 💳\nUser: show me the steps to open an acount\n    User baseline (advisory communication context only; use only when clearly\n    relevant to the current request and never as factual banking evidence):\n    None\n    Financial subqueries: [{\"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"customer_component\": \"What are the steps to open a Horizon bank account?\"}]\n    Non-financial conversational attention cues (tone only; never evidence, a banking request, a tool input, or customer-facing source text): []\n    Answerable evidence by retrieval task: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\", \"resolved_request\": \"What are the steps to open a Horizon bank account?\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"content\": \"Question: Why did Horizon Bank reject my credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Every credit card request undergoes an internal review, and we evaluate each submission thoroughly. Typical reasons for a denial include:\\n- Insufficient earnings:\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_001}}‑{{faq_1b9ab045_002}} with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_003}}\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_004}}+ with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_005}}\\n  • Non‑resident ({{faq_1b9ab045_006}} years or older) earning less than {{faq_1b9ab045_007}} annually\\n- Having already reached the maximum credit exposure allowed across all banks\\n- Existing overdue obligations with other financial institutions\\n- Absence of a recent Notice of Assessment or CPF contribution record\\n- Applicant is younger than {{faq_1b9ab045_008}} years old\\n\\nIf you were declined, you may still consider opening a Horizon savings account, which offers up to {{faq_1b9ab045_009}} p.a. on the first {{faq_1b9ab045_010}} deposited and can provide up to an {{faq_1b9ab045_011}} return when paired with a Horizon debit card (subject to terms and conditions). To start the savings account application, simply:\\n- Uninstall the Horizon App\\n- Re‑install the Horizon App from the app store\\n- Submit a savings‑account request through the app\\n\\nPlease note that Singapore‑dollar deposits held by non‑bank depositors are protected by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation up to {{faq_1b9ab045_012}} per depositor across all Scheme members, as mandated by law.\"}]}]\n    Validated tool results: [{\"tool_task_id\": \"tool_rag_1\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"tool_name\": \"rag\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"approved_result\": {\"search_task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_70aebcd6\", \"faq_1b9ab045\"]}]}, \"availability_reason\": \"\"}]\n    Enabled future capabilities: [{\"tool_name\": \"rag\", \"operations\": [\"retrieve_faq_evidence\"], \"description\": \"Retrieve and verify Horizon FAQ and policy evidence.\", \"read_only\": true}, {\"tool_name\": \"service_request\", \"operations\": [\"register_service_request\"], \"description\": \"Register a guided, multi-step form for an approved low- or intermediate-risk service request (e.g. address update, card replacement, KYC document resubmission). Never used for money movement or high-risk actions -- those are deeplink's job.\", \"read_only\": false, \"available_requests\": [{\"service_request_id\": \"profile-address-update\", \"description\": \"Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\", \"risk_level\": \"low\"}, {\"service_request_id\": \"card-replacement-request\", \"description\": \"Request a replacement physical card for a non-fraud reason (worn or damaged).\", \"risk_level\": \"low\"}, {\"service_request_id\": \"kyc-document-resubmission\", \"description\": \"Resubmit an identity document for an existing customer's KYC record.\", \"risk_level\": \"intermediate\"}]}]\n    Intent clarification inputs: []\n    Terminal unresolved retrieval tasks (semantic anchors only; NOT answer evidence): []\n    Declined inputs: []\n\n    \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n\n    Rules:\n    - First decide resolution_status. Return NEEDS_TOOLS only when a supplied\n      financial subquery has a concrete unresolved need that an enabled,\n      registered capability could materially address and which does not\n      duplicate a completed, unavailable, failed, blocked, pending, or running\n      tool task. RAG internal retries are already complete at this point; do\n      not request RAG again for a terminal RAG result.\n    - A capability's own description can scope out specific reasons or\n      situations, not just name a general topic -- match on the whole\n      description, not the nearest keyword. For example, a capability\n      described as covering card replacement \"for a non-fraud reason (worn\n      or damaged)\" does not cover a lost or stolen card, even though both\n      are \"card replacement\" in general terms; do not propose a tool_gap for\n      a capability whose stated scope excludes the customer's actual\n      situation. When every registered capability's scope excludes the\n      situation, that is EXHAUSTED for this need, not NEEDS_TOOLS -- approved\n      RAG evidence, if any, may still answer it on its own.\n    - Return RESOLVED when current approved evidence and safe clarification\n      anchors are enough to form the response. Return EXHAUSTED when a gap\n      remains but no enabled non-duplicate capability can address it.\n    - RAG evidence and a registered capability are independent coverage\n      decisions for the same subquery, not alternatives to choose between.\n      Decide each on its own merits: does approved evidence precisely and\n      completely answer what the customer asked, and, separately, does a\n      registered enabled capability's own description precisely match the\n      action the customer is asking to take? Answering yes to the\n      capability question always adds that tool_gap — with no exception,\n      including when RAG evidence is itself a complete, well-grounded,\n      directly-on-topic answer (for example, FAQ steps that correctly\n      explain how to update an address manually in the app). Being able to\n      explain how a customer could perform an action themselves is never a\n      substitute for being able to perform that same action for them\n      through a registered capability — the capability is strictly more\n      valuable, not an alternative path to the same outcome, so its\n      existence is never a reason to omit the tool_gap. Include both\n      `validated_task_ids` and the `tool_gaps` entry in that case; the\n      response generator can present the RAG evidence as useful reference\n      alongside the offered capability. Evidence that describes a related\n      but different action (for example, general personal-details updates\n      when the customer asked specifically about resubmitting an identity\n      document) is adjacent context, an even weaker case than a precise\n      answer, and must never be the reason a matching capability is left\n      out either.\n    - A tool gap is an