{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T17:18:01.923+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_f94eea34-9fd5-4774-8324-bb3efb37b7b2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): show my credit bill\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: show my credit bill\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Access the mobile application dashboard and select the credit card account to view recent billing statements.\", \"policy\": \"Monthly billing statements are generated on the statement date and are available for download in PDF format.\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card statement is a summary of all transactions, payments, and interest charges for a billing cycle.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"Retrieve and display the current credit card statement or bill.\", \"direct_query\": \"Retrieve and display the current credit card statement or bill.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Access the mobile application dashboard and select the credit card account to view recent billing statements.\", \"policy\": \"Monthly billing statements are generated on the statement date and are available for download in PDF format.\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card statement is a summary of all transactions, payments, and interest charges for a billing cycle.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss card details, card replacement, and payment recipient information, but none provide information on how to retrieve or view credit card billing statements.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_12b5523e\", \"content\": \"Question: I submitted an online application for a Horizon credit card. Where can I view the complete details of my Horizon account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Install the Horizon App on your device and sign in using MyInfo. Ensure your MyInfo profile is fully set up for a seamless first login.\\n- After logging in, the Horizon App provides full control over your credit card, allowing you to:\\n  - Review card information such as number, expiration date, and CVV\\n  - Activate the newly issued physical card\\n  - Lock or unlock the card as needed\\n  - Add the card to Apple Wallet\\n  - Request a change to your credit limit\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_75b5beb8\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I determine when my Horizon Bank credit card statements are generated and when payments are due?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we calculate your credit card statement and repayment dates from the issuance date of your digital Horizon card. Typically, you can expect your first statement to be available within {{faq_75b5beb8_001}} to {{faq_75b5beb8_002}} days, and your first repayment will be due between {{faq_75b5beb8_003}} to {{faq_75b5beb8_004}} days after card issuance. For instance, if your card was issued on March {{faq_75b5beb8_005}}, {{faq_75b5beb8_006}}, and you've chosen a monthly repayment schedule on the {{faq_75b5beb8_007}}th, your initial statement might be ready by April {{faq_75b5beb8_008}}, {{faq_75b5beb8_009}}, with the first payment due on April {{faq_75b5beb8_010}}, {{faq_75b5beb8_011}}. To find these dates, follow these simple steps:\\n   * Log in to your Horizon App\\n   * Navigate to the 'Credit Card' section\\n   * Click on 'Statements' to view your upcoming payment due date and the date of your next statement\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_23b30ec5\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I access key information about my Horizon card, including the card number, expiration date, and security code?\\n\\nAnswer: To retrieve your Horizon card details, simply follow these steps: \\n      * Launch the Horizon App on your device\\n      * Navigate to the 'Account Overview' section\\n      * Select 'Card Information' to view your card details, including the card number, expiry date, and CVV\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7672e1dd\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for paying my Horizon credit card bill?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Using a Horizon savings account**\\n  - Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  - Navigate to **Money** → **Credit Card** → **Pay credit card**.\\n  - Your Horizon Savings account will appear; pick it from the list.\\n  - Verify the payment details and swipe up to authorise.\\n  - For guidance on funding your Horizon Savings account, visit: https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/savings-account/#how-do-i-deposit-money-into-my-savings-account\\n\\n- **Using accounts at other banks**\\n  You may settle your Horizon credit card bill from another bank either by adding the card number as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient. Below are the typical flows for major Singapore banks.\\n\\n  **DBS/POSB**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_001}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open **Pay & Transfer** > **Local** > **Add Local Recipient** > **Bank Account**.\\n  - Input the recipient name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your {{faq_7672e1dd_002}}‑digit Horizon card number as the account number.\\n  - Confirm the details and add the recipient (additional verification may be required).\\n  - Return to **Pay & Transfer** > **Local**, choose your Horizon card, enter the amount, ensure **FAST** is enabled, and proceed.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_003}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_004}} working days)*\\n  - Go to **Pay & Transfer** > **Cards** > **Add Credit Card Recipient**.\\n  - Provide your {{faq_7672e1dd_005}}‑digit Horizon card number, select card type **Singapore – VISA/MasterCard**, and fill in your name.\\n  - After adding, select the card under **Cards**, input the payment amount, and confirm.\\n\\n  **UOB**\\n  - Choose **Pay & Transfer** > **Other Accounts / Cards** > **New Transfer**.\\n  - Under **Bank Account / Other Institutions**, pick “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and enter your {{faq_7672e1dd_006}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Specify the amount and swipe to submit.\\n\\n  **OCBC**\\n  - Tap **Local Transfers** > **Account Number** > **Add payee**.\\n  - Enter the payee name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your Horizon card number (use your initials for the reference).\\n  - After adding, wait roughly {{faq_7672e1dd_007}} hours for the payee to become active, then initiate a local transfer to the card and confirm.\\n\\n  **Standard Chartered Bank Singapore**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_008}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open the menu > **Transfer & Payments** > **Local Transfer**.\\n  - Add a new payee, choose **Local**, enter “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and your {{faq_7672e1dd_009}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Authenticate with your {{faq_7672e1dd_010}}‑digit PIN and confirm.\\n  - Select the newly added Horizon card as the destination, enter the amount, and swipe to complete.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_011}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_012}} working days)*\\n  - Menu > **Transfers & Payments** > **Add & Manage Biller** > **Other Bank’s Credit Card Payee**.\\n  - Provide the cardholder name and your Horizon card number, then continue.\\n  - After confirming the payee, enter your PIN, choose **Move My Money**, pick **Pay Other Bank Credit Cards**, select the Horizon card as the payee, specify the source account and amount, and finalize.\\n\\n  For any bank not listed, you can still add your Horizon card number either as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient; processing typically takes about {{faq_7672e1dd_013}} working days.\\n\\n  **Important note**: If you hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card, ensure the card is paired with the savings account before using the paired‑payment method. Details on pairing are available at https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/credit-card/#how-does-the-card-pairing-work.\\n\\n  Failure to pay by the due date may result in a late‑payment fee and interest on the outstanding balance. Making only the minimum payment also incurs interest on the remaining amount. For full terms, consult the Horizon FAQs or the customer T&Cs on the website or app.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing