 on 'View'.\\n      * Locate and tap the 'Disable AutoPay' button to cancel the automatic payment arrangement. \\n      Note that if the linked savings account is closed, any scheduled automatic payments will be automatically terminated, and no further payments will be processed.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3e533fdb\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's automatic payment feature work for my credit card and savings accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our automated payment system allows you to set up recurring transfers from your Horizon savings account to your Horizon credit card, other savings accounts, or even credit cards held with other banks. This feature also enables you to make one-off or recurring payments using PayNow on specified future dates. To utilize this service, simply choose your preferred payment amount, frequency, and duration, including the start and end dates. For recurring credit card payments, the system will automatically deduct the funds from your Horizon savings account two days before the payment is due, ensuring timely settlements.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repea