{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T17:38:49.683+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_f94eea34-9fd5-4774-8324-bb3efb37b7b2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): How do I pay my credit card bill?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: How do I change my residential address?\nAI: You can update your residential address directly using the Change Address option below.\nUser: How do I pay my credit card bill?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Log in to the mobile app, select your credit card account, and choose the bill payment option.\", \"policy\": \"Payments must be made by the statement due date to avoid late fees and interest charges.\", \"conceptual\": \"Credit card bill payment is the process of settling your outstanding balance using funds from your account.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"How do I pay my credit card bill?\", \"direct_query\": \"How do I pay my credit card bill?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Log in to the mobile app, select your credit card account, and choose the bill payment option.\", \"policy\": \"Payments must be made by the statement due date to avoid late fees and interest charges.\", \"conceptual\": \"Credit card bill payment is the process of settling your outstanding balance using funds from your account.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_e6cc390d\", \"faq_3e533fdb\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_e6cc390d\", \"faq_3e533fdb\"], \"reason\": \"The provided parents offer information on how to manage automatic payments and set up recurring transfers for credit card bills, which are relevant aspects of the payment process, but they do not provide a general, manual, one-time payment procedure for a credit card bill.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_e6cc390d\", \"fact\": \"Automatic payment features for a Horizon Bank credit card can be disabled by navigating to the credit card section in the Horizon App and selecting the Disable AutoPay button.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3e533fdb\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank's automated payment system allows for recurring transfers from a Horizon savings account to a credit card, with funds deducted two days before the payment due date.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7672e1dd\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for paying my Horizon credit card bill?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Using a Horizon savings account**\\n  - Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  - Navigate to **Money** → **Credit Card** → **Pay credit card**.\\n  - Your Horizon Savings account will appear; pick it from the list.\\n  - Verify the payment details and swipe up to authorise.\\n  - For guidance on funding your Horizon Savings account, visit: https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/savings-account/#how-do-i-deposit-money-into-my-savings-account\\n\\n- **Using accounts at other banks**\\n  You may settle your Horizon credit card bill from another bank either by adding the card number as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient. Below are the typical flows for major Singapore banks.\\n\\n  **DBS/POSB**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_001}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open **Pay & Transfer** > **Local** > **Add Local Recipient** > **Bank Account**.\\n  - Input the recipient name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your {{faq_7672e1dd_002}}‑digit Horizon card number as the account number.\\n  - Confirm the details and add the recipient (additional verification may be required).\\n  - Return to **Pay & Transfer** > **Local**, choose your Horizon card, enter the amount, ensure **FAST** is enabled, and proceed.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_003}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_004}} working days)*\\n  - Go to **Pay & Transfer** > **Cards** > **Add Credit Card Recipient**.\\n  - Provide your {{faq_7672e1dd_005}}‑digit Horizon card number, select card type **Singapore – VISA/MasterCard**, and fill in your name.\\n  - After adding, select the card under **Cards**, input the payment amount, and confirm.\\n\\n  **UOB**\\n  - Choose **Pay & Transfer** > **Other Accounts / Cards** > **New Transfer**.\\n  - Under **Bank Account / Other Institutions**, pick “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and enter your {{faq_7672e1dd_006}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Specify the amount and swipe to submit.\\n\\n  **OCBC**\\n  - Tap **Local Transfers** > **Account Number** > **Add payee**.\\n  - Enter the payee name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your Horizon card number (use your initials for the reference).\\n  - After adding, wait roughly {{faq_7672e1dd_007}} hours for the payee to become active, then initiate a local transfer to the card and confirm.\\n\\n  **Standard Chartered Bank Singapore**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_008}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open the menu > **Transfer & Payments** > **Local Transfer**.\\n  - Add a new payee, choose **Local**, enter “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and your {{faq_7672e1dd_009}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Authenticate with your {{faq_7672e1dd_010}}‑digit PIN and confirm.\\n  - Select the newly added Horizon card as the destination, enter the amount, and swipe to complete.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_011}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_012}} working days)*\\n  - Menu > **Transfers & Payments** > **Add & Manage Biller** > **Other Bank’s Credit Card Payee**.\\n  - Provide the cardholder name and your Horizon card number, then continue.\\n  - After confirming the payee, enter your PIN, choose **Move My Money**, pick **Pay Other Bank Credit Cards**, select the Horizon card as the payee, specify the source account and amount, and finalize.\\n\\n  For any bank not listed, you can still add your Horizon card number either as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient; processing typically takes about {{faq_7672e1dd_013}} working days.\\n\\n  **Important note**: If you hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card, ensure the card is paired with the savings account before using the paired‑payment method. Details on pairing are available at https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/credit-card/#how-does-the-card-pairing-work.\\n\\n  Failure to pay by the due date may result in a late‑payment fee and interest on the outstanding balance. Making only the minimum payment also incurs interest on the remaining amount. For full terms, consult the Horizon FAQs or the customer T&Cs on the website or app.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7d56cd4e\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for configuring automatic payments from my Horizon Bank savings account to pay my Horizon credit card bill on a recurring basis?\\n\\nAnswer: To establish automatic recurring payments for your Horizon credit card from your Horizon Bank savings account, follow these steps: \\n   - Access your Horizon App and navigate to the 'Credit Card' section, then select 'Pay card' and choose 'Horizon Credit Card'. \\n   - Initiate the AutoPay setup by either tapping on the 'Set up' option from the AutoPay banner or by going to 'Payments', then 'AutoPay', and selecting 'New AutoPay' followed by 'Horizon Credit Card'. \\n   - Determine the repayment amount type, choosing between the statement balance or the minimum balance, to schedule your future repayments. \\n   - Confirm your selection by choosing 'Schedule AutoPay'. \\n   Please note that for recurring AutoPay transfers to your Horizon credit card, the payment will be automatically deducted from your Horizon savings account {{faq_7d56cd4e_001}} days prior to the payment due date.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_a5ab2ed8\", \"content\": \"Question: What methods are available for settling my Horizon Bank credit card account, and what are the associated timelines and potential fees?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we offer multiple convenient options for paying your credit card bill. You can pay directly from your Horizon Bank savings account through the Horizon App by following these steps:\\n   * Log in to the Horizon App and navigate to the 'Money' section.\\n   * Select 'Credit Card' and then 'Pay credit card'.\\n   * Choose your savings account from the available options to complete the payment.\\n   * Review the transfer details carefully before confirming the transaction.\\n\\n   Alternatively, you can pay using other bank accounts. This can be done in two main ways: by adding your Horizon credit card as a local transfer recipient or as a credit card payment recipient. The steps may vary depending on your bank's app, but generally, you will need to add your Horizon credit card details as a new payee or recipient and then initiate the transfer.\\n\\n   For payments made through other banks' apps, the processing time may take up to {{faq_a5ab2ed8_001}} working days. It's essential to note that your credit card payment is due on the date you selected when you first applied for your Horizon credit card. Failure to make payment by the due date may result in late payment fees and interest on the outstanding amount. Even if you make the minimum payment on time, you will still be charged interest on the remaining balance.\\n\\n   For detailed instructions on paying through specific banks like DBS/POSB, UOB, OCBC, and Standard Chartered Bank, as well as information on card pairing for Trust Link credit card holders, please refer to our FAQs on the Horizon Bank website or through the Horizon App. Remember, timely payments help you avoid additional fees and interest charges.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_da1c24c4\", \"content\": \"Question: How do I lower the credit limit on my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App and tap **Profile** > **Settings**\\n- Select the **Decrease credit limit** option\\n- Drag the slider to the amount you prefer and confirm the adjustment\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e6cc390d\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps can I take to cancel the automatic payment feature on my Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To deactivate the automatic payment feature for your Horizon Bank credit card, please follow these steps: \\n      * Log in to your Horizon App and navigate to the credit card section.\\n      * Select the 'Pay card' option and proceed to the AutoPay settings by clicking on 'View'.\\n      * Locate and tap the 'Disable AutoPay' button to cancel the automatic payment arrangement. \\n      Note that if the linked savings account is closed, any scheduled automatic payments will be automatically terminated, and no further payments will be processed.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3e533fdb\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's automatic payment feature work for my credit card and savings accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our automated payment system allows you to set up recurring transfers from your Horizon savings account to your Horizon credit card, other savings accounts, or even credit cards held with other banks. This feature also enables you to make one-off or recurring payments using PayNow on specified future dates. To utilize this service, simply choose your preferred payment amount, frequency, and duration, including the start and end dates. For recurring credit card payments, the system will automatically deduct the funds from your Horizon savings account two days before the payment is due, ensuring timely settlements.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n        