{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T17:38:53.164+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_f94eea34-9fd5-4774-8324-bb3efb37b7b2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    GLOBAL RESPONSE SUFFICIENCY & TOOL RESOLUTION\n    You are an internal resolution controller for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ\n    assistant. Decide only whether the complete validated outcome is ready for\n    customer response generation, requires one further enabled capability, or\n    is exhausted. You do NOT write customer-facing text or plan UI.\n\n    Customer request: How do I pay my credit card bill?\n    Trusted conversation context (use only to understand the customer's current\n    meaning, priority, and references; never as factual banking evidence):\n    Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: How do I change my residential address?\nAI: You can update your residential address directly using the Change Address option below.\nUser: How do I pay my credit card bill?\n    User baseline (advisory communication context only; use only when clearly\n    relevant to the current request and never as factual banking evidence):\n    None\n    Financial subqueries: [{\"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"customer_component\": \"How do I pay my credit card bill?\"}]\n    Non-financial conversational attention cues (tone only; never evidence, a banking request, a tool input, or customer-facing source text): []\n    Answerable evidence by retrieval task: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\", \"resolved_request\": \"How do I pay my credit card bill?\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7672e1dd\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for paying my Horizon credit card bill?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Using a Horizon savings account**\\n  - Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  - Navigate to **Money** → **Credit Card** → **Pay credit card**.\\n  - Your Horizon Savings account will appear; pick it from the list.\\n  - Verify the payment details and swipe up to authorise.\\n  - For guidance on funding your Horizon Savings account, visit: https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/savings-account/#how-do-i-deposit-money-into-my-savings-account\\n\\n- **Using accounts at other banks**\\n  You may settle your Horizon credit card bill from another bank either by adding the card number as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient. Below are the typical flows for major Singapore banks.\\n\\n  **DBS/POSB**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_001}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open **Pay & Transfer** > **Local** > **Add Local Recipient** > **Bank Account**.\\n  - Input the recipient name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your {{faq_7672e1dd_002}}‑digit Horizon card number as the account number.\\n  - Confirm the details and add the recipient (additional verification may be required).\\n  - Return to **Pay & Transfer** > **Local**, choose your Horizon card, enter the amount, ensure **FAST** is enabled, and proceed.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_003}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_004}} working days)*\\n  - Go to **Pay & Transfer** > **Cards** > **Add Credit Card Recipient**.\\n  - Provide your {{faq_7672e1dd_005}}‑digit Horizon card number, select card type **Singapore – VISA/MasterCard**, and fill in your name.\\n  - After adding, select the card under **Cards**, input the payment amount, and confirm.\\n\\n  **UOB**\\n  - Choose **Pay & Transfer** > **Other Accounts / Cards** > **New Transfer**.\\n  - Under **Bank Account / Other Institutions**, pick “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and enter your {{faq_7672e1dd_006}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Specify the amount and swipe to submit.\\n\\n  **OCBC**\\n  - Tap **Local Transfers** > **Account Number** > **Add payee**.\\n  - Enter the payee name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your Horizon card number (use your initials for the reference).\\n  - After adding, wait roughly {{faq_7672e1dd_007}} hours for the payee to become active, then initiate a local transfer to the card and confirm.\\n\\n  **Standard Chartered Bank Singapore**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_008}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open the menu > **Transfer & Payments** > **Local Transfer**.\\n  - Add a new payee, choose **Local**, enter “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and your {{faq_7672e1dd_009}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Authenticate with your {{faq_7672e1dd_010}}‑digit PIN and confirm.\\n  - Select the newly added Horizon card as the destination, enter the amount, and swipe to complete.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_011}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_012}} working days)*\\n  - Menu > **Transfers & Payments** > **Add & Manage Biller** > **Other Bank’s Credit Card Payee**.\\n  - Provide the cardholder name and your Horizon card number, then continue.\\n  - After confirming the payee, enter your PIN, choose **Move My Money**, pick **Pay Other Bank Credit Cards**, select the Horizon card as the payee, specify the source account and amount, and finalize.\\n\\n  For any bank not listed, you can still add your Horizon card number either as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient; processing typically takes about {{faq_7672e1dd_013}} working days.\\n\\n  **Important note**: If you hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card, ensure the card is paired with the savings account before using the paired‑payment method. Details on pairing are available at https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/credit-card/#how-does-the-card-pairing-work.\\n\\n  Failure to pay by the due date may result in a late‑payment fee and interest on the outstanding balance. Making only the minimum payment also incurs interest on the remaining amount. For full terms, consult the Horizon FAQs or the customer T&Cs on the website or app.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_a5ab2ed8\", \"content\": \"Question: What methods are available for settling my Horizon Bank credit card account, and what are the associated timelines and potential fees?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we offer multiple convenient options for paying your credit card bill. You can pay directly from your Horizon Bank savings account through the Horizon App by following these steps:\\n   * Log in to the Horizon App and navigate to the 'Money' section.\\n   * Select 'Credit Card' and then 'Pay credit card'.\\n   * Choose your savings account from the available options to complete the payment.\\n   * Review the transfer details carefully before confirming the transaction.\\n\\n   Alternatively, you can pay using other bank accounts. This can be done in two main ways: by adding your Horizon credit card as a local transfer recipient or as a credit card payment recipient. The steps may vary depending on your bank's app, but generally, you will need to add your Horizon credit card details as a new payee or recipient and then initiate the transfer.\\n\\n   For payments made through other banks' apps, the processing time may take up to {{faq_a5ab2ed8_001}} working days. It's essential to note that your credit card payment is due on the date you selected when you first applied for your Horizon credit card. Failure to make payment by the due date may result in late payment fees and interest on the outstanding amount. Even if you make the minimum payment on time, you will still be charged interest on the remaining balance.\\n\\n   For detailed instructions on paying through specific banks like DBS/POSB, UOB, OCBC, and Standard Chartered Bank, as well as information on card pairing for Trust Link credit card holders, please refer to our FAQs on the Horizon Bank website or through the Horizon App. Remember, timely payments help you avoid additional fees and interest charges.\"}]}]\n    Validated tool results: [{\"tool_task_id\": \"tool_deeplink_2\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"tool