{"timestamp": "2026-08-25T03:38:03.037+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_d1718d1a-d7ec-4ed5-97cf-346ace8ce2a3", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): What's my address on file, and what loyalty tier am I on?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: please show me the cuurent address in my profile\nAI: I can prepare a summary for a human agent to review your request.\nUser: What's my address on file, and what loyalty tier am I on?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Check your current loyalty tier status by logging into the rewards dashboard section\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tier status is determined by monthly transaction volume and account balance thresholds\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers provide tiered access to exclusive rewards, bonus points, and promotional offers\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Rewards_Program\", \"target_intent\": [\"Rewards And Promotions\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the current loyalty tier status for the customer?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the current loyalty tier status for the customer?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Check your current loyalty tier status by logging into the rewards dashboard section\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tier status is determined by monthly transaction volume and account balance thresholds\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers provide tiered access to exclusive rewards, bonus points, and promotional offers\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_8065dd4a\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps can I take to integrate my loyalty program membership with the Horizon Bank partner merchant application?\\n\\nAnswer: To establish a connection between your membership and the partner app, kindly refer to the comprehensive guide available at the Horizon Bank support portal, which outlines the straightforward process for linking your accounts and unlocking exclusive rewards.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0a4686e9\", \"content\": \"Question: If I change a voucher’s status to 'Redeemed' in the Horizon app, what will occur?\\n\\nAnswer: • After you set a coupon or voucher to 'Redeemed', its status is updated and it no longer appears on the active Rewards dashboard or in the My Coupons section.\\n• The item remains accessible in the 'Redeemed/Expired' tab for reference.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5a7395a4\", \"content\": \"Question: How do I qualify for and receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on my FairPrice Group purchases made with my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be eligible for the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on your FairPrice Group spend, you must first meet the minimum monthly spend requirement for three consecutive months, starting from the month your Horizon card is approved. The required spend amounts are {{faq_5a7395a4_001}} for NTUC Link Credit cardholders, {{faq_5a7395a4_002}} for Horizon Link Credit cardholders, or {{faq_5a7395a4_003}} for NTUC Link Debit and Horizon Link Debit cardholders, based on the posting date of your transactions. Once you've met this condition, you'll receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on all your posted FairPrice Group spend. Additionally, if you meet the higher minimum monthly spend of {{faq_5a7395a4_004}} for NTUC Link Credit and Horizon Link Credit cardholders, or {{faq_5a7395a4_005}} for NTUC Link Debit and Horizon Link Debit cardholders, you'll be eligible for an extra quarterly bonus. The FairPrice Group spend includes purchases made at FairPrice, FairPrice Finest, FairPrice Xtra, FairPrice Online, Warehouse Club, Unity, and Cheers stores, as well as participating Kopitiam stalls, excluding FairPrice Xpress and Cheers outlets within Esso stations. You will receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on your FairPrice Group spend once the transactions are posted in the month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_13c2c54b\", \"content\": \"Question: I've noticed that I can save or unsave certain digital vouchers through the Horizon App, but not all of them. What determines which ones I can manage?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we offer two categories of digital coupons to our customers. The first category is universally available and can be saved or removed from your account at your discretion. The second category consists of exclusive, award-based coupons that are issued to customers who meet specific eligibility criteria. Once you've been awarded one of these exclusive coupons, it will remain in your account until its expiration date, as it cannot be manually removed.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the