us for the customer?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Check your current loyalty tier status by logging into the rewards dashboard section\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tier status is determined by monthly transaction volume and account balance thresholds\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers provide tiered access to exclusive rewards, bonus points, and promotional offers\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Navigate to the profile settings menu to view your registered residential address and contact details\", \"policy\": \"Address updates require verification through secure channels to ensure account security and regulatory compliance\", \"conceptual\": \"Maintaining accurate personal information is essential for receiving important bank correspondence and security notifications\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss loyalty program integration, voucher management, and bonus point eligibility criteria, but none of these documents explain how a customer can check their current loyalty tier status or what that status is.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss general product offerings, coupon locations, and rewards program integration, but none of these documents explain how a customer can check their current loyalty tier status or what that status is.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss Horizon Bank's naming, mobile-first platform, referral codes, and PayNow transaction updates. None of these documents contain information regarding how to check a loyalty tier status or what the current loyalty tier status is for the customer.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_ed92e41d\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps can I take to confirm that an email claiming to be from Horizon Bank is authentic?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank will only send messages from an address that finishes with @horizonbank.sg.  \\n- We will never request your password, PIN, or any confidential account details via email.  \\n- If you are unsure about a message, reach out to our Customer Care team at +{{faq_ed92e41d_001}} {{faq_ed92e41d_002}}- HORIZ ( +{{faq_ed92e41d_003}} {{faq_ed92e41d_004}} {{faq_ed92e41d_005}} ) or connect with us through the in‑app chat or a phone call.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_2cadcac6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information will be displayed to someone attempting to send me funds through the Horizon Bank PayNow service?\\n\\nAnswer: When an individual initiates a transaction using your PayNow proxy, they will be presented with a masked version of your name, ensuring your privacy is maintained throughout the payment process.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b7fc742\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for checking the Linkpoints I have accumulated through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To access your earned Linkpoints, follow these straightforward steps: \\n      * Launch the Horizon App and sign in to your account\\n      * Navigate to the main 'Dashboard' section\\n      * Click on 'Rewards' to view your available rewards\\n      * Choose 'Link Rewards' to see the specifics of your earned Linkpoints\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7fc44444\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank collaborate with regulatory bodies to combat cyber threats and protect customers from fraudulent activities?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we are committed to safeguarding our customers' interests through a collaborative approach with the Monetary Authority of Singapore and other relevant authorities. The Shared Responsibility Framework is a pivotal initiative that underscores the importance of joint efforts between banks, regulatory bodies, and customers in preventing and mitigating the impact of scams. This framework specifically addresses vulnerabilities that scammers may exploit, including impersonation of legitimate entities, such as government agencies or financial institutions like Horizon Bank, where fraudsters deceive customers into divulging sensitive information. Additionally, it tackles the risks associated with malicious links sent via digital platforms, which can lead to the compromise of account credentials. By promoting a culture of shared responsibility, we aim to empower our customers with the knowledge and best practices necessary to secure their financial information and transactions, thereby fostering a safer digital banking environment for all.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual