stomer's KYC record.\", \"risk_level\": \"intermediate\"}]}, {\"tool_name\": \"api\", \"operations\": [\"read_customer_data\"], \"description\": \"Read one specific, verified piece of the customer's own banking data on file (e.g. their address, their loyalty tier). Use this for a request about the customer's actual personal data value, not a general policy or procedure question -- that is RAG's job.\", \"read_only\": true, \"available_fields\": [{\"field_id\": \"profile-address\", \"description\": \"The customer's current postal address on file.\", \"disclosure_mode\": \"placeholder\"}, {\"field_id\": \"loyalty-status\", \"description\": \"The customer's current loyalty program tier.\", \"disclosure_mode\": \"direct_value\"}]}, {\"tool_name\": \"deeplink\", \"operations\": [\"resolve_navigation\"], \"description\": \"Return a validated Horizon navigation destination. Use this when the customer needs to navigate to a specific screen in the app.\", \"read_only\": true, \"available_destinations\": [{\"destination_id\": \"card-management\", \"description\": \"View & Manage Card screen — freeze, replace, enable overseas usage.\", \"route\": \"/app/cards/manage\", \"label\": \"Manage Card\"}, {\"destination_id\": \"account-statements\", \"description\": \"Statements screen — view and download past monthly statements.\", \"route\": \"/app/accounts/statements\", \"label\": \"View Statements\"}, {\"destination_id\": \"profile-personal-details\", \"description\": \"Profile -> Personal Details screen — view and edit name, address, phone, email.\", \"route\": \"/app/profile/personal-details\", \"label\": \"Update Profile\"}, {\"destination_id\": \"security-settings\", \"description\": \"Profile -> Security screen — update PIN, view Horizon Key status.\", \"route\": \"/app/profile/security\", \"label\": \"Security Settings\"}, {\"destination_id\": \"pay-credit-card-bill\", \"description\": \"Pay Credit Card Bill screen — pay outstanding balance from a savings account.\", \"route\": \"/app/cards/pay\", \"label\": \"Pay Bill\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Create only additive tasks. Never recreate a completed, unavailable,\n          failed, blocked, or pending task.\n        - Every task must reference exactly one supplied subquery_id.\n        - Use only an enabled tool_name and one of its listed operations.\n        - Do not create a task merely to restate, search again, or rewrite a\n          completed result. Do not invent facts, customer data, or capabilities.\n        - RAG's internal retries are not outer tool tasks. Add RAG only when\n          no RAG task for that subquery has already reached a terminal state.\n        - Return no task if no registered enabled capability can close a gap.\n        - For tool_name \"service_request\", input must use the literal key\n          \"service_request_id\". Choose the best-fitting id from that tool's\n          available_requests in the registry. Never invent an id or include form fields.\n        - For tool_name \"deeplink\", input must use the literal key\n          \"destination_id\". Example: {\"destination_id\": \"card-management\"}.\n          Use deeplinks to navigate the user to specific screens in the app\n          (e.g., manage card, view statements) based on the available_destinations\n          in the registry. A deeplink will be substituted into a button for the\n          user to click.\n        - For tool_name \"api\", input must use the literal key \"field_id\".\n          Example: {\"field_id\": \"profile-address\"}. Choose only from the\n          available_fields listed for \"api\" in the registry. Use \"api\" only\n          when the customer is asking for one specific, personal,\n          account-linked data value of their own on file (e.g. \"what's my\n          address on file\", \"what's my loyalty tier\") -- never for a general\n          policy, procedure, or \"how do I...\" question, which is RAG's job.\n        - Read the full description of each registry entry before choosing one.\n          If the customer's actual situation falls outside every candidate's stated\n          scope, do not create a task for it at all.\n\n        Output JSON only:\n        {\"tool_tasks\":[{\"subquery_id\":\"...\",\"tool_name\":\"...\",\"operation\":\"...\",\"input\":{}}]}\n        "}
