{"timestamp": "2026-08-25T04:29:33.895+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_96d7d668-9f1a-49e9-98e1-f608cb8531de", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): What's my address on file, and what loyalty tier am I on?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Ben! How can I help with your banking today?\n\nYou can fulfil these requests using the forms below.\nUser: What's my address on file, and what loyalty tier am I on?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Navigate to profile settings to view or update the current residential address details on file\", \"policy\": \"Registered address must be a valid residential location supported by official government issued identification documents\", \"conceptual\": \"The registered address is the primary contact location used for all official bank correspondence and statements\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Horizon_APP\", \"target_intent\": [\"Profile Updates\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the customer's registered address on file?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the customer's registered address on file?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Navigate to profile settings to view or update the current residential address details on file\", \"policy\": \"Registered address must be a valid residential location supported by official government issued identification documents\", \"conceptual\": \"The registered address is the primary contact location used for all official bank correspondence and statements\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_6e2d941d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for changing my home address when applying for a Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Singapore citizens and Permanent Residents (effective {{faq_6e2d941d_001}} Oct {{faq_6e2d941d_002}})**: All address modifications must be submitted through Singpass. Steps:\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_003}}. Sign in to Singpass and choose your language.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_004}}. Verify that the details entered in your Horizon Bank application are accurate before proceeding.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_005}}. Submit the request; ICA will mail a {{faq_6e2d941d_006}}‑digit PIN to your new residence.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_007}}. For local addresses, the PIN letter typically arrives within one week.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_008}}. Use the PIN to continue your Horizon Bank onboarding via the ICA e‑Service portal. (Further guidance available via the provided link.)\\n- **Non‑Singapore residents**:\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_009}}*: Access the myTax Portal with your Singpass or Singpass Foreign Account (SFA), select “Update Contact Details,” and amend your residential or mailing address. The update is reflected within three business days. (More information at the linked page.)\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_010}}*: Go to the Ministry of Manpower (MoM) website and follow these actions:\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_011}}. Click “Log in for EP Online with Singpass” under the pass‑holder section.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_012}}. Log in using your Singpass credentials.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_013}}. Choose “Change Particulars – Personal Contact Details and Residential Address of Pass Holder.”\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_014}}. Input your Main Pass ID and search.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_015}}. Edit the residential postal address and save the changes.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Check current loyalty status by logging into the rewards dashboard within the mobile banking application\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tier status is determined by monthly transaction volume and total assets held with the bank\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers provide tiered access to exclusive rewards, preferential interest rates, and dedicated customer service support\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Rewards_Program\", \"target_intent\": [\"Rewards And Promotions\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the customer's current loyalty tier?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the customer's current loyalty tier?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Check current loyalty status by logging into the rewards dashboard within the mobile banking application\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tier status is determined by monthly transaction volume and total assets held with the bank\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers provide tiered access to exclusive rewards, preferential interest rates, and dedicated customer service support\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_8065dd4a\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps can I take to integrate my loyalty program membership with the Horizon Bank partner merchant application?\\n\\nAnswer: To establish a connection between your membership and the partner app, kindly refer to the comprehensive guide available at the Horizon Bank support portal, which outlines the straightforward process for linking your accounts and unlocking exclusive rewards.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5a7395a4\", \"content\": \"Question: How do I qualify for and receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on my FairPrice Group purchases made with my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be eligible for the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on your FairPrice Group spend, you must first meet the minimum monthly spend requirement for three consecutive months, starting from the month your Horizon card is approved. The required spend amounts are {{faq_5a7395a4_001}} for NTUC Link Credit cardholders, {{faq_5a7395a4_002}} for Horizon Link Credit cardholders, or {{faq_5a7395a4_003}} for NTUC Link Debit and Horizon Link Debit cardholders, based on the posting date of your transactions. Once you've met this condition, you'll receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on all your posted FairPrice Group spend. Additionally, if you meet the higher minimum monthly spend of {{faq_5a7395a4_004}} for NTUC Link Credit and Horizon Link Credit cardholders, or {{faq_5a7395a4_005}} for NTUC Link Debit and Horizon Link Debit cardholders, you'll be eligible for an extra quarterly bonus. The FairPrice Group spend includes purchases made at FairPrice, FairPrice Finest, FairPrice Xtra, FairPrice Online, Warehouse Club, Unity, and Cheers stores, as well as participating Kopitiam stalls, excluding FairPrice Xpress and Cheers outlets within Esso stations. You will receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on your FairPrice Group spend once the transactions are posted in the month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_13c2c54b\", \"content\": \"Question: I've noticed that I can save or unsave certain digital vouchers through the Horizon App, but not all of them. What determines which ones I can manage?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we offer two categories of digital coupons to our customers. The first category is universally available and can be saved or removed from your account at your discretion. The second category consists of exclusive, award-based coupons that are issued to customers who meet specific eligibility criteria. Once you've been awarded one of these exclusive coupons, it will remain in your account until its expiration date, as it cannot be manually removed.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0a4686e9\", \"content\": \"Question: If I change a voucher’s status to 'Redeemed' in the Horizon app, what will occur?\\n\\nAnswer: • After you set a coupon or voucher to 'Redeemed', its status is updated and it no longer appears on the active Rewards dashboard or in the My Coupons section.\\n• The item remains accessible in the 'Redeemed/Expired' tab for reference.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For