nquiries\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is my current loyalty tier?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is my current loyalty tier?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"View current loyalty status through the rewards dashboard in the mobile application\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tier upgrades are calculated based on monthly transaction volume and account balances\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers represent the membership level determining eligibility for exclusive rewards and promotional benefits\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Check the specific savings plan details to identify applicable base and bonus interest rate structures\", \"policy\": \"Interest rates are determined by meeting specific monthly transaction volume and average daily balance conditions\", \"conceptual\": \"Savings account interest rates vary based on the selected plan and current account activity requirements\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_353df275\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss how to link accounts and general rewards program information, but none provide the customer's current loyalty tier or a mechanism to retrieve it beyond a general reference to the mobile app.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_da866599\", \"fact\": \"Rewards membership is integrated with the Horizon card upon approval.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss PayNow changes, rewards account merging, Link account integration, and digital coupon management. None of these parents provide information regarding the customer's current loyalty tier or the interest rate for their savings account.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_353df275\"], \"reason\": \"The provided parents contain detailed information regarding the interest rates for the Horizon Bank Savings Account, which addresses the second part of the user's query. However, none of the provided parents contain information on how the customer can retrieve their current loyalty tier status, as they only describe the requirements to qualify for the premium tier.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_353df275\", \"fact\": \"Interest rates for savings accounts are determined by the specific savings plan, with the Signature plan offering base and bonus interest rates based on transaction and balance conditions.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_a3bab790\", \"fact\": \"Customers are automatically upgraded to the premium tier for three months when their combined average daily balance and investment value reaches a specific threshold.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_bf86ef1f\", \"content\": \"Question: How is the interest on a Horizon Bank Savings Account calculated and what can I expect to earn?\\n\\nAnswer: The return you receive depends on the savings plan attached to your account. If you have not selected a specific plan, Horizon Bank automatically enrolls you in the Signature plan. Under this plan you can earn up to {{faq_bf86ef1f_001}} per annum on the first {{faq_bf86ef1f_002}} of your savings balance, broken down as follows:\\n- **Base rate:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_003}} p.a. – applies to all balances without any conditions.\\n- **Spend‑bonus:**\\n  - {{faq_bf86ef1f_004}} p.a. for members of the Horizon Union, provided you complete at least five qualifying card purchases in the month.\\n  - {{faq_bf86ef1f_005}} p.a. for non‑Union members, also requiring five qualifying transactions.\\n- **Balance‑bonus:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_006}} p.a. when your average daily balance for the month reaches {{faq_bf86ef1f_007}} or more.\\n- **Salary‑bonus:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_008}} p.a. if you receive a minimum salary credit of {{faq_bf86ef1f_009}} in a single GIRO transaction (purpose code SALA) during the month.\\nAny amount exceeding {{faq_bf86ef1f_010}} earns only the base rate of {{faq_bf86ef1f_011}} p.a. Interest is posted on the final day of each month.\\n\\n**Illustrative calculation (December, {{faq_bf86ef1f_012}}‑day month):**\\nAssume you maintain a daily balance of {{faq_bf86ef1f_013}}, complete five qualifying card purchases of at least {{faq_bf86ef1f_014}} each on {{faq_bf86ef1f_015}} Dec, and have a {{faq_bf86ef1f_016}} salary credit on {{faq_bf86ef1f_017}} Dec.\\n- **Union member scenario**\\n  - Base on first {{faq_bf86ef1f_018}} M: {{faq_bf86ef1f_019}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_020}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_021}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_022}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_023}}\\n  - Spend‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_024}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_025}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_026}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_027}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_028}}\\n  - Balance‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_029}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_030}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_031}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_032}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_033}}\\n  - Salary‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_034}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_035}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_036}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_037}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_038}}\\n  - Base on excess {{faq_bf86ef1f_039}}: {{faq_bf86ef1f_040}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_041}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_042}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_043}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_044}}\\n  - **Total interest:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_045}}\\n- **Non‑Union member scenario**\\n  - Base on first {{faq_bf86ef1f_046}} M: {{faq_bf86ef1f_047}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_048}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_049}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_050}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_051}}\\n  - Spend‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_052}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_053}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_054}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_055}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_056}}\\n  - Balance‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_057}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_058}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_059}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_060}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_061}}\\n  - Salary‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_062}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_063}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_064}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_065}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_066}}\\n  - Base on excess {{faq_bf86ef1f_067}}: {{faq_bf86ef1f_068}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_069}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_070}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_071}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_072}}\\n  - **Total interest:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_073}}\\n\\nThese figures are simplified for demonstration purposes.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_23772469\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank calculate interest for Savings Pots?\\n\\nAnswer: - Money placed in your Savings Pots earns interest at the same rate as the balance in your primary Horizon Bank account.\\n- Interest is computed on the aggregate of your main account and all Savings Pots, using the prevailing rate.\\n- The resulting interest is credited to your main account at the close of each month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_90e0db65\", \"content\": \"Question: What interest rate does Horizon Bank apply to Savings Pots?\\n\\nAnswer: - Money placed in Horizon Savings Pots earns interest at the same rate as the balance in your primary Horizon account.\\n- The bank calculates interest on the aggregate of your main account and Savings Pots using the current rate, and credits the earned amount to your main account at the close of each month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7b5e0f27\", \"content\": \"Question: What three savings‑plan choices does Horizon Bank provide for its deposit accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank now lets you select a savings plan that determines the interest applied to the balance in your savings account. The three available options are **Signature**, **Zen**, and **Flex**.\\n- You may switch your plan at any time before the month ends; the new selection takes effect on the {{faq_7b5e0f27_001}}st day of the following month.\\n- Each successful change triggers an in‑app push notification and an email alert.\\n- To see which plan is currently active, open the **Horizon App**, navigate to **Savings > Interest This Month**, where you can also monitor your progress toward any bonus interest tied to the chosen plan.\\n- If you do not make a change during a given month, the existing plan automatically rolls over into the next month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_353df275\", \"content\": \"Question: What interest can I expect to earn on a Horizon Bank Savings Account?\\n\\nAnswer: - The rate you receive is tied to the savings plan you are enrolled in. If you have not selected a plan, Horizon Bank automatically places you in the Signature plan.\\n- Under the Signature plan you may earn a combined interest of up to {{faq_353df275_001}} per annum on the first {{faq_353df275_002}} of your savings balance. The rate is broken down as follows:\\n  * Base interest: {{faq_353df275_003}} p.a. (no conditions).\\n  * Spend bonus: {{faq_353df275_004}} p.a. for Horizon Union members or {{faq_353df275_005}} p.a. for non‑members, provided you complete at least five qualifying card transactions each month.\\n  * Balance bonus: {{faq_353df275_006}} p.a. when your average daily balance for the month reaches {{faq_353df275_007}}.\\n  * Salary bonus: {{faq_353df275_008}} p.a. if a minimum salary credit of {{faq_353df275_009}} is posted in a single GIRO transaction with purpose code SALA during the month.\\n- Any amount above {{faq_353df275_010}} accrues only the base rate of {{faq_353df275_011}} p.a.\\n- Interest is credited on the last day of each month.\\n\\n**Illustrative example (December, {{faq_353df275_012}}‑day month)**\\nAssume you maintain a daily balance of {{faq_353df275_013}}, execute five qualifying card purchases of at least {{faq_353df275_014}} each on {{faq_353df275_015}} Dec, and receive a {{faq_353df275_016}} salary credit on {{faq_353df275_017}} Dec.\\n\\n*For Horizon Union members:*\\n  - Base on first {{faq_353df275_018}} M: {{faq_353df275_019}} × {{faq_353df275_020}} × {{faq_353df275_021}}/{{faq_353df275_022}} = {{faq_353df275_023}}\\n  - Spend bonus: {{faq_353df275_024}} × {{faq_353df275_025}} × {{faq_353df275_026}}/{{faq_353df275_027}} = {{faq_353df275_028}}\\n  - Balance bonus: {{faq_353df275_029}} × {{faq_353df275_030}} × {{faq_353df275_031}}/{{faq_353df275_032}} = {{faq_353df275_033}}\\n  - Salary bonus: {{faq_353df275_034}} × {{faq_353df275_035}} × {{faq_353df275_036}}/{{faq_353df275_037}} = {{faq_353df275_038}}\\n  - Base on excess {{faq_353df275_039}}: {{faq_353df275_040}} × {{faq_353df275_041}} × {{faq_353df275_042}}/{{faq_353df275_043}} = {{faq_353df275_044}}\\n  - **Total interest = {{faq_353df275_045}}**\\n\\n*For non‑Union members:*\\n  - Base on first {{faq_353df275_046}} M: {{faq_353df275_047}} × {{faq_353df275_048}} × {{faq_353df275_049}}/{{faq_353df275_050}} = {{faq_353df275_051}}\\n  - Spend bonus: {{faq_353df275_052}} × {{faq_353df275_053}} × {{faq_353df275_054}}/{{faq_353df275_055}} = {{faq_353df275_056}}\\n  - Balance bonus: {{faq_353df275_057}} × {{faq_353df275_058}} × {{faq_353df275_059}}/{{faq_353df275_060}} = {{faq_353df275_061}}\\n  - Salary bonus: {{faq_353df275_062}} × {{faq_353df275_063}} × {{faq_353df275_064}}/{{faq_353df275_065}} = {{faq_353df275_066}}\\n  - Base on excess {{faq_353df275_067}}: {{faq_353df275_068}} × {{faq_353df275_069}} × {{faq_353df275_070}}/{{faq_353df275_071}} = {{faq_353df275_072}}\\n  - **Total interest = {{faq_353df275_073}}**\\n\\n*Note: The figures above are simplified for illustration purposes.*\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]}\n        "}
