_069}} × {{faq_353df275_070}}/{{faq_353df275_071}} = {{faq_353df275_072}}\\n  - **Total interest = {{faq_353df275_073}}**\\n\\n*Note: The figures above are simplified for illustration purposes.*\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5a7395a4\", \"content\": \"Question: How do I qualify for and receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on my FairPrice Group purchases made with my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be eligible for the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on your FairPrice Group spend, you must first meet the minimum monthly spend requirement for three consecutive months, starting from the month your Horizon card is approved. The required spend amounts are {{faq_5a7395a4_001}} for NTUC Link Credit cardholders, {{faq_5a7395a4_002}} for Horizon Link Credit cardholders, or {{faq_5a7395a4_003}} for NTUC Link Debit and Horizon Link Debit cardholders, based on the posting date of your transactions. Once you've met this condition, you'll receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on all your posted FairPrice Group spend. Additionally, if you meet the higher minimum monthly spend of {{faq_5a7395a4_004}} for NTUC Link Credit and Horizon Link Credit cardholders, or {{faq_5a7395a4_005}} for NTUC Link Debit and Horizon Link Debit cardholders, you'll be eligible for an extra quarterly bonus. The FairPrice Group spend includes purchases made at FairPrice, FairPrice Finest, FairPrice Xtra, FairPrice Online, Warehouse Club, Unity, and Cheers stores, as well as participating Kopitiam stalls, excluding FairPrice Xpress and Cheers outlets within Esso stations. You will receive the quarterly bonus Linkpoints on your FairPrice Group spend once the transactions are posted in the month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7b5e0f27\", \"content\": \"Question: What three savings‑plan choices does Horizon Bank provide for its deposit accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank now lets you select a savings plan that determines the interest applied to the balance in your savings account. The three available options are **Signature**, **Zen**, and **Flex**.\\n- You may switch your plan at any time before the month ends; the new selection takes effect on the {{faq_7b5e0f27_001}}st day of the following month.\\n- Each successful change triggers an in‑app push notification and an email alert.\\n- To see which plan is currently active, open the **Horizon App**, navigate to **Savings > Interest This Month**, where you can also monitor your progress toward any bonus interest tied to the chosen plan.\\n- If you do not make a change during a given month, the existing plan automatically rolls over into the next month.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"procedural\": \"Check your specific account interest rate by selecting the account details view in the app\", \"policy\": \"Interest rates are calculated based on the daily balance and credited to the account monthly\", \"conceptual\": \"The savings account interest rate represents the annual percentage yield earned on your deposited funds\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Interest And Rates\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the interest rate for the customer's savings account?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the interest rate for the customer's savings account?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_3\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Check your specific account interest rate by selecting the account details view in the app\", \"policy\": \"Interest rates are calculated based on the daily balance and credited to the account monthly\", \"conceptual\": \"The savings account interest rate represents the annual percentage yield earned on your deposited funds\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_0b62be43\", \"content\": \"Question: Does Horizon Bank currently provide a promotional interest rate for its Savings Account?\\n\\nAnswer: - At present, Horizon Bank does not offer a promotional interest rate for its Savings Account.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to