{"timestamp": "2026-08-25T10:22:16.219+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_cc62ff70-479d-4c0f-9a59-a2e53f4ab230", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): What's my address on file, and what loyalty tier am I on? and what's interest rate for my saving account\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Ben! How can I help with your banking today?\n\nYou can fulfil these requests using the forms below.\n\nWould you like to continue updating your address, and do you still want to complete your pending requests for Change Address and Resubmit KYC Document?\nUser: What is my current loyalty tier, and what is the interest rate for my savings account?\nAI: Your current loyalty tier is Gold 🌟. Regarding your savings account interest rate, the rate you receive is tied to the savings plan you are enrolled in. If you have not selected a plan, Horizon Bank automatically places you in the Signature plan. Under the Signature plan, you may earn a combined interest of up to 1% per annum (yearly interest expressed as a percentage of your balance) on the first S$1,200,000 of your savings balance. At present, Horizon Bank does not offer a promotional interest rate for its Savings Account.\nUser: What's my address on file, and what loyalty tier am I on? and what's interest rate for my saving account\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Update your registered residential address by logging into the mobile app profile settings menu\", \"policy\": \"Customers must provide valid proof of residence documentation to verify any changes to address\", \"conceptual\": \"The registered address is the primary location used for all official bank correspondence and statements\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Deposit_Account\", \"Horizon_APP\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the address on file for the customer?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the address on file for the customer?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Update your registered residential address by logging into the mobile app profile settings menu\", \"policy\": \"Customers must provide valid proof of residence documentation to verify any changes to address\", \"conceptual\": \"The registered address is the primary location used for all official bank correspondence and statements\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Navigate to the profile section to view current residential details stored in our secure database\", \"policy\": \"Verification of identity is required before displaying sensitive personal information like your registered home address\", \"conceptual\": \"Bank records maintain a single official residential address for all account correspondence and regulatory compliance purposes\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents describe the procedure for changing an address, but do not contain information regarding the customer's current address on file.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_6e2d941d\", \"fact\": \"Address modifications for Singapore residents must be submitted through Singpass.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents describe how to locate account numbers and statements, but do not contain information regarding the customer's current address on file.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents describe how to locate statements, referral codes, and payment information, but none contain information regarding the customer's registered address on file.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_24568045\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for changing my personal details—address, phone number, or email—within the Horizon ecosystem?\\n\\nAnswer: - Updating your personal information can now be done directly through the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_002}}. Tap the Profile icon located at the upper‑right corner.\\n{{faq_24568045_003}}. Within Profile, navigate to Settings ► Personal Details.\\n{{faq_24568045_004}}. Choose the field you wish to modify (address, phone number, or email).\\n{{faq_24568045_005}}. For phone number or email changes, enter the one‑time password (OTP) sent to you.\\n{{faq_24568045_006}}. Provide your Horizon Key for additional verification before the update is applied.\\n{{faq_24568045_007}}. After you submit, the change will be processed within {{faq_24568045_008}} hours for phone numbers and email addresses, while address updates take effect instantly.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_29a71c6f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I take if the data pulled from MyInfo is incorrect?\\n\\nAnswer: - Update your personal details via Singpass.\\n- Wait between {{faq_29a71c6f_001}} and {{faq_29a71c6f_002}} hours for the changes to propagate before re‑submitting your request.\\n- Verify that the address listed in MyInfo is a Singapore address.\\n- Note that for Singapore citizens and permanent residents, address updates may require additional time to appear in MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_11305460\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I change personal information such as my NRIC/FIN, nationality, name, or the name embossed on my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: - To modify details like NRIC/FIN, nationality, legal name, or the card‑embossing name, reach out to Horizon Customer Care via the Horizon app’s call or chat function. Expect a response within roughly three business days.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c0c586c8\", \"content\": \"Question: I’ve already linked my mobile number (or NRIC) to another bank for PayNow receipts. Can I also associate that same mobile number with my Horizon Bank account for PayNow?\\n\\nAnswer: - Yes, you may. However, you must first remove the existing association of your mobile number (or NRIC) with the other bank’s account before linking it to your Horizon Bank account.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"View your current loyalty status and progress toward the next tier within the rewards dashboard\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tiers are determined by total monthly transaction volume and average daily account balances maintained\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers provide tiered access to exclusive banking benefits and enhanced reward point earning rates\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Rewards_Program\", \"ALL\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Authentication And Security\", \"Features And Limits\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Account Management\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the customer's current loyalty tier?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the customer's current loyalty tier?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"View your current loyalty status and progress toward the next tier within the rewards dashboard\", \"policy\": \"Loyalty tiers are determined by total monthly transaction volume and average daily account balances maintained\", \"conceptual\": \"Loyalty tiers provide tiered access to exclusive banking benefits and enhanced reward point earning rates\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Check the rewards summary page to identify your active membership level and associated program benefits\", \"policy\": \"Eligibility for higher loyalty tiers is recalculated automatically based on your monthly banking activity and balances\", \"conceptual\": \"Membership tiers define the specific multiplier for reward points earned on eligible daily banking transactions\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss savings plans, interest rates, and loyalty program integration, but do not contain information about the customer's current loyalty tier.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss the rewards program and voucher management, but do not contain information regarding the customer's current loyalty tier.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss the bank's history, branding, and security frameworks, but do not contain information regarding the customer's current loyalty tier.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_da866599\", \"content\": \"Question: As a current member of the rewards program, will my existing membership automatically connect to my Horizon Bank card?\\n\\nAnswer: Indeed, upon approval of your application, your existing rewards membership will be seamlessly integrated with your new Horizon card. This integration enables you to accumulate rewards points through your debit or credit card transactions and conveniently monitor your points balance and transaction history within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_560b6fac\", \"content\": \"Question: I'm an existing Horizon Bank rewards member, but my new Horizon card is linked to a freshly created account. How can I ensure my previously accumulated rewards are preserved?\\n\\nAnswer: To safeguard your existing rewards balance, kindly contact the Horizon Bank Customer Support Team through their dedicated web portal to seek assistance and guidance on merging your accounts.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_31afb42a\", \"content\": \"Question: If I currently have a Link account connected to my existing rewards card, will applying for a Horizon Bank Link card cause any disruptions to my rewards balance or transactions?\\n\\nAnswer: Upon successful application for your Horizon card, your Link account will seamlessly integrate with your new Horizon Link card, allowing you to view your Linkpoints balance and transaction history within the Horizon App. For detailed information on Link rewards, NTUC benefits, or Visa card perks, please visit the Link Rewards website. Alternatively, you can contact the Customer Care Team through the webform available at https://support.link.sg/hc/en-us/requests/new for personalized assistance.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b7fc742\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for checking the Linkpoints I have accumulated through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To access your earned Linkpoints, follow these straightforward steps: \\n      * Launch the Horizon App and sign in to your account\\n      * Navigate to the main 'Dashboard' section\\n      * Click on 'Rewards' to view your available rewards\\n      * Choose 'Link Rewards' to see the specifics of your earned Linkpoints\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidenc