ly supported by the Permitted Evidence above; nothing\n    outside it may be used as a factual source.\n\n    The \"facts\" list is a set of pre-verified statements about this specific request's outcome; the content may state any of them directly, in its own natural phrasing, without needing further support. The content must not state or imply anything beyond what the facts list says -- no approval, no guarantee, no outcome or actor the facts do not name.\n\n    Output JSON only:\n    {\"evidence_grounded\": true/false, \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_violations\": [{\"scope\": \"...\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim phrase\"], \"evidence_gap\": \"...\"}]}\n    "}
