{"timestamp": "2026-08-26T01:42:31.583+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_52ae10f5-85a0-40a8-b6ff-fe0af548cec7", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): i want to check my credit line\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Ben! How can I help with your banking today?\n\nYou can fulfil your request using the form below.\n\nIt looks like you have a pending request to change your address; would you still like to complete that?\nUser: i want to check my credit line\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"View current credit line balance through the account dashboard or mobile application settings menu\", \"policy\": \"Credit line limits are subject to periodic review based on account activity and repayment history\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit line is a flexible borrowing limit that allows access to funds up to a maximum amount\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Personal_Loan\", \"Credit_Card\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"Check the available credit line limit.\", \"direct_query\": \"Check the available credit line limit.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"View current credit line balance through the account dashboard or mobile application settings menu\", \"policy\": \"Credit line limits are subject to periodic review based on account activity and repayment history\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit line is a flexible borrowing limit that allows access to funds up to a maximum amount\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Navigate to the credit summary section within the secure portal to view your current available credit\", \"policy\": \"The bank reserves the right to adjust your total credit line based on ongoing risk assessment criteria\", \"conceptual\": \"Your available credit represents the remaining portion of your approved limit that you can currently access\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss credit limits in the context of loan applications, balance transfers, and instant loan eligibility, but none provide information on how a customer can check their current available credit line balance.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss Instant Loan application processes, credit card interest rates, and loan fees, but none contain information on how a customer can check their current available credit line balance.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents explain how to request a credit limit increase or decrease, but none provide information on how a customer can view or check their current available credit line balance.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_618e0d95\", \"content\": \"Question: How does being classified as a regulated customer influence my borrowing capacity at Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: As a regulated customer of Horizon Bank, your overall credit limit for unsecured credit facilities, including those from other financial institutions, will be subject to certain restrictions. Specifically, for Singapore citizens and permanent residents, the total credit limit will be capped as follows: \\n   - If your annual income falls within the range of {{faq_618e0d95_001}} to less than {{faq_618e0d95_002}}, your credit limit will be up to {{faq_618e0d95_003}} months' worth of your income.\\n   - For individuals aged {{faq_618e0d95_004}} and above with an annual income of less than {{faq_618e0d95_005}}, the credit limit will be limited to up to {{faq_618e0d95_006}} months' income.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_742db265\", \"content\": \"Question: How does my existing credit limit with another bank impact my Horizon Bank credit card application as a regulated customer?\\n\\nAnswer: When applying for a Horizon Bank credit card, your overall credit limit is considered across all unsecured credit facilities, including those with other banks. For instance, if your monthly income is {{faq_742db265_001}}, your total credit limit would be {{faq_742db265_002}}, which is four times your monthly income. If you have an existing credit limit of {{faq_742db265_003}} with another bank, Horizon Bank can offer you a credit limit of up to {{faq_742db265_004}}. To determine your credit limit, you can either allow Horizon Bank to decide or choose your own credit limit. To explore these options in more detail, consider the following steps:\\n   * To have Horizon Bank determine your credit limit, review the assigned limit and adjust as needed.\\n   * To select your own credit limit, which may be higher than the assigned limit, follow the prompts to input your preferred amount.\\n   * If you are satisfied with the assigned credit limit, simply confirm and proceed with your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e3c2064e\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for obtaining a complimentary credit report from Horizon Bank after applying for a credit card or credit limit increase?\\n\\nAnswer: To receive a free credit report, you can access it within {{faq_e3c2064e_001}} calendar days of your credit card application or credit limit increase approval or rejection via the designated credit bureau's website. Alternatively, you may visit the credit bureau's office in person, presenting your approval or rejection email along with your identification documents, such as your NRIC or passport. For existing Horizon Bank credit card holders applying for an additional card, simply present the required documents at the credit bureau's office to obtain your complimentary report. The credit bureau's details are as follows: Credit Bureau (Singapore) Pte Ltd, located at {{faq_e3c2064e_002}} Shenton Way, #{{faq_e3c2064e_003}}-{{faq_e3c2064e_004}} SGX Centre {{faq_e3c2064e_005}}, Singapore {{faq_e3c2064e_006}}, or visit their website at www.creditbureau.com.sg for more information.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_47df6d92\", \"content\": \"Question: What happens if I change my mind about a credit limit increase I've already requested through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: Please note that once you've submitted a request to increase your credit limit, it cannot be withdrawn. You will receive updates on the status of your request via push notifications in the Horizon App and email. However, if you later decide you'd like to reduce your credit limit, you have the option to do so by selecting 'Decrease credit limit' directly within the Horizon App.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]}\n        "}
