{"timestamp": "2026-08-26T01:42:37.066+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_52ae10f5-85a0-40a8-b6ff-fe0af548cec7", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        INCREMENTAL TOOL-CALLING PLANNER\n        You must plan tool tasks to address the customer's financial subqueries.\n        For each subquery listed under \"Subqueries with a remaining gap this\n        round\" below, decide which registered, enabled tool(s) are\n        genuinely RELEVANT -- whose own description actually matches what\n        the customer needs -- and propose a task for each one that applies.\n        Judge relevance only; do not weigh cost yourself.\n\n        Tool cost characteristics (for the \"rag_role\" decision below only):\n        - \"api\", \"deeplink\", and \"service_request\" are each a single,\n          deterministic operation -- effectively free once dispatched.\n        - \"rag\" requires an internal iterative retrieval process that can\n          take several rounds and several model calls to converge -- the\n          only tool with real cost.\n\n        Financial subqueries: [{\"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"customer_component\": \"Check the available credit line limit.\"}]\n        Subqueries with a remaining gap this round: [\"subquery_1\"]\n        Validated terminal tool results: [{\"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"tool_name\": \"rag\", \"status\": \"unavailable\", \"result\": {}, \"availability_reason\": \"No approved FAQ evidence resolved this financial subquery.\"}]\n        Enabled tool registry: [{\"tool_name\": \"rag\", \"operations\": [\"retrieve_faq_evidence\"], \"description\": \"Retrieve and verify Horizon FAQ and policy evidence.\", \"read_only\": true}, {\"tool_name\": \"service_request\", \"operations\": [\"register_service_request\"], \"description\": \"Register a guided, multi-step form for an approved low- or intermediate-risk service request (e.g. address update, card replacement, KYC document r