ature of your account. 💳\n\nIf you'd like to check details regarding potential late payment charges, you can visit our dedicated webpage.\nUser: Just to confirm, what's the yearly cost of keeping this credit card open?\n    User baseline (advisory communication context only; use only when clearly\n    relevant to the current request and never as factual banking evidence):\n    None\n    Non-financial conversational attention cues (tone only; not evidence, a banking request, or customer-facing source text):\n    [\"customer seeking confirmation of previously provided information\"]\n    Global resolution context (internal coverage and unresolved-topic anchors\n    only; not evidence, response wording, or UI guidance):\n    {\"subquery_status\": {\"subquery_1\": \"RESOLVED\"}}\n    Approved evidence by retrieval task: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_request\": \"What is the annual fee for my credit card?\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_3bade286\", \"content\": \"Question: Do the zero-fee benefits associated with my Horizon card have an expiration date?\\n\\nAnswer: As a valued Horizon Bank customer, you can rest assured that the zero-fee privileges, including no annual fee, foreign transaction fee, card replacement fee, or overlimit fee, are a permanent feature of your account. For details regarding potential late payment charges, please visit our dedicated webpage.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e5db6d91\", \"content\": \"Question: Are there any fees associated with obtaining a supplementary Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank does not levy any issuance or annual fees for an additional card. All expenses incurred on the supplementary card are combined with the primary card’s balance, and any late‑payment penalties or interest charges are applied exclusively to the main cardholder.\"}]}]\n    Intent clarification inputs: []\n    Terminal unresolved task markers (topic/status only; never evidence): []\n    Decline inputs: []\n    Available shortc